---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="Why G-IRB exists — a structured knowledge base on internal ratings-based models.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Why this site exists</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Whether it is new guidelines concerning model development, changes to the CRR, or
        best practice in machine learning methods, the IRB landscape keeps evolving at a
        rapid pace. Keeping up with it is one problem; retaining what you worked out last
        time is a different and harder one.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is an answer to the second problem &mdash; cognitive offloading. A
        structured space to capture, clarify and revisit what gets learned across projects,
        regulations and technical methodologies, written to be re-read rather than read once.
      </p>
      <p>
        It now serves a dual purpose: a knowledge base for ongoing learning, and a resource
        for anyone else working with IRB models. The subjects are PD, LGD and EAD model
        development, regulatory interpretation, and machine learning applications.
      </p>

      <h2>A note on the explainers</h2>
      <p>
        Wherever a topic is easier to understand by moving it than by reading about it,
        there is an interactive figure instead of a static chart. Everything runs in your
        browser, so you can push the inputs to places a worked example would not go, and
        the arithmetic is left visible rather than hidden behind a result.
      </p>

      <h2>Scope and disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is illustrative. Nothing substitutes for the regulation itself,
        nothing constitutes advice, and nothing represents the view of any employer or
        institution. Where a figure reproduces a regulatory formula it is stated plainly
        which article it comes from, so you can go and check it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Errors are mine. If you find one, the source is public &mdash; corrections are
        welcome.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: 48px 72px; }
  .head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding-bottom: 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-bottom: 34px; }
</style>
